{"series":{"id":"organ-donation-residence::organ-recipients-all","label":"Transplant recipients · All · state of residence","dataset_id":"frozen-atlas","unit":"transplant recipients (HRSA person count)","scope":"us_states","definition":"HRSA overview count of individuals receiving one or more transplants during the calendar year, classified by recipient state of residence. These are recipient counts, not counts of organs, procedures or operations at centers in the state. Organ category: All. All is the publisher's aggregate category; do not sum organ-specific people counts to recreate it.","denominator":"None; published absolute count. Not population-standardized or risk-adjusted.","reporting_period":"Calendar year 2025; workbook refreshed October 23, 2026","source_url":"https://data.hrsa.gov/DataDownload/DD_Files/Organ_Donation_and_Transplantation_Data.xlsx","sources":[{"id":"hrsa-organ-puf","title":"HRSA Organ Donation and Transplantation public-use workbook","url":"https://data.hrsa.gov/DataDownload/DD_Files/Organ_Donation_and_Transplantation_Data.xlsx","date":"Refreshed October 23, 2026; selected calendar year 2025","note":"Overview - State provides native state-of-residence person counts. HRSA data rows cover January 2021–March 2026. The workbook READ ME date-range table is stale (2019–2024); use the individual data-row refresh/range fields. Counts suppressed for privacy remain missing.","license":"Public HRSA download; source dashboard states usage limitations: none. Attribution retained; no separate machine-readable license supplied."},{"id":"hrsa-organ-definitions","title":"HRSA Organ Donation and Transplantation dashboard definitions and suppression FAQ","url":"https://data.hrsa.gov/Content/Documents/topics/Organ%20Donation%20and%20Transplantation%20Dashboard%20FAQs.pdf","date":"Retrieved October 28, 2026","note":"Definitions distinguish people, registrations, organs and transplant-center geography. Primary and secondary suppression mean a suppressed cell is not necessarily 1–15.","license":"Public U.S. government explanatory document; attribution retained."}],"limitations":["The map uses individual state of residence, not the location of the recovery hospital, OPO headquarters or transplant center. People may receive care across state borders.","These are absolute activity/person counts; differences also reflect population size, medical need, referral and listing practices, access, and other factors. The maps do not rank care quality or outcomes.","Deceased and living donors, organs recovered or transplanted, transplant recipients and waitlist candidates are different measures. A donor can supply multiple organs; recipient and donor counts cannot be equated.","Waitlist candidates here are individuals added during the year, not current or year-end waitlist stock and not the number of registrations. A candidate may have multiple registrations.","Organ categories overlap at the person level. Kidney-Pancreas is a separate source category. Do not sum organ categories, donor types or other distinct-person measures to claim a unique overall population.","HRSA suppresses small nonzero counts and additional secondary cells. Suppressed values are null, not zero, and are not assigned a guessed range. Explicit published zeros remain zero.","Complete-year maps use 2025. The raw file also contains 2026 through March 31 only. Counts are subject to later corrections; a lower partial-year number is not an annual decline.","Intestine and some rare-organ categories are not exposed as state-specific rows in this dashboard release. Their absence is not zero activity.","Donor registration or authorization is not measured here. The data do not establish willingness to donate, an individual treatment recommendation, or the effect of a policy."],"interval_type":null,"display_reference":null,"years":[2025],"places":[{"id":"AL","name":"Alabama"},{"id":"AK","name":"Alaska"},{"id":"AZ","name":"Arizona"},{"id":"AR","name":"Arkansas"},{"id":"CA","